40308154 Quagga 0.99.19 AS-path confederation use-after-free

Backport of upstream Quagga commit:
https://github.com/Quagga/quagga/commit/5552da8f9abd786fb76019135277003f489626d6
Author: Paul Jakma <paul.jakma@hpe.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jun 2016 11:36:59 +0100
Subject: bgpd: Fix use after free in aspath_prepend with confeds

Confederation deletion can free the cached head segment and leave an empty
path.  Reload the head and handle an empty result before comparing types
or merging segments.  Refreshed against Oracle's Quagga 0.99.19 source;
comments and whitespace follow the component's existing style.

--- bgpd/bgp_aspath.c
+++ bgpd/bgp_aspath.c
@@ -1227,6 +1227,15 @@
   if (seg1->type == AS_SEQUENCE && seg2->type == AS_CONFED_SEQUENCE)
     as2 = aspath_delete_confed_seq (as2);
 
+  /* Confederation deletion may have freed the original head segment. */
+  seg2 = as2->segments;
+  if (seg2 == NULL)
+    {
+      as2->segments = assegment_dup_all (as1->segments);
+      aspath_str_update (as2);
+      return as2;
+    }
+
   /* Compare last segment type of as1 and first segment type of as2. */
   if (seg1->type != seg2->type)
     return aspath_merge (as1, as2);
